    "seasonalWindow": {
      "start": "04-01",
      "endExclusive": "06-01"
    },
    "qualityFiltering": "Per composite pixel, kept only if SummaryQA = 0 (good data) and DetailedQA bits 8 (adjacent cloud), 10 (mixed clouds), 14 (possible snow/ice) and 15 (possible shadow) are all 0, and the raw NDVI lies in -2000..10000 (this excludes the fill value). Nothing is gap-filled or interpolated.",
    "temporalAggregation": "Composites whose start date lies in [04-01, 06-01) of each year (end exclusive) are selected. Per pixel, the mean of the valid composites is taken; the regional value is then the mean over pixels, so every pixel has equal weight regardless of how many composites it had. A 16-day composite that starts in the window may extend a few days past its end date.",
    "spatialAggregation": "Circle of radius 10 km (geodesic buffer) around the point, sampled at 250 m nominal resolution in the dataset's native sinusoidal projection (native pixel ~231.7 m). Identical for every location in a comparison.",
    "acceptanceRules": "A year is reported only if at least 50% of the region's pixels have a valid observation and valid pixels average at least 2 valid composites; otherwise the year is null with a stated reason. Regions with >=50 % open water are reported as unsuitable.",
    "limitations": [
      "NDVI is a greenness indicator derived from red and near-infrared reflectance. It is not a measurement of vegetation area, biomass, desertification or vegetation loss.",
      "No land-cover classification is applied: cropland, built-up areas, bare ground and natural vegetation inside the circle are averaged together.",
      "The April-June window is the same at every latitude and is not a growing season everywhere (for example the Southern Hemisphere autumn/winter, or high latitudes).",
      "Water is detected from one composite's land/water flag; seasonal or ephemeral water may be missed.",
      "Interannual NDVI differences can reflect cloud/aerosol residue, sensor and compositing effects, phenology timing and rainfall, not only land-surface change."
    ]
  }
